e, the equation of the axis of symmetry is $x=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561017 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083186 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "205ecbfe-49fd-559f-a4e7-a36900f1d9c7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Axis of Symmetry of a Parabola"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "366f61ee-82b5-511f-9834-78fe121c414a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560484} {:answer/id #uuid "404b7834-6467-595c-8689-798a9dd0ba2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560507} {:answer/id #uuid "b1fbd0b0-1be4-52eb-a17b-70d994f0ef95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560722} {:answer/id #uuid "dace083e-ae80-5311-9205-e754e34dc1f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560793} {:answer/id #uuid "df7c299f-a11e-5927-ad5b-bcd08a02bd4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560804}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df7c299f-a11e-5927-ad5b-bcd08a02bd4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560804} :answer-field/id #uuid "58080bed-1ac2-5652-ab76-b460fa71e917" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560898}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7a249418-3166-5952-aa2e-ffdd779176d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-106539" :question/problem "Find the axis of symmetry for the parabola $y=2{x}^{2}+8x-3.$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=a{x}^{2}+bx+c$ is given by\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{b}{2a}.\n$$\n\nWe substitute $a=2$ and $b=8$ into the formula for the axis of symmetry. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-\\frac{8}{2(2)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{4} \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the axis of symmetry is $x=-2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186560993 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083186 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "205ecbfe-49fd-559f-a4e7-a36900f1d9c7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Axis of Symmetry of a Parabola"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "037caabe-2f41-51bc-8802-582169729c0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560367} {:answer/id #uuid "0c3f92cf-9ad6-5ac6-bcf8-367dd8ea8269" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560392} {:answer/id #uuid "6c7d6dad-f969-5f91-a45e-3d713c825d49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560592} {:answer/id #uuid "b38332e4-d6a6-57fc-ab73-bece0af7380c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560726} {:answer/id #uuid "b6f6c486-0a93-53b2-b1e7-f096d03aa4fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560731}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b38332e4-d6a6-57fc-ab73-bece0af7380c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560726} :answer-field/id #uuid "367bd5f7-e5a7-580c-976d-0f5f94cccf47" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560885}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3f0e7d2f-2da0-5cf5-aa62-0f9950fe080c" :question/math-academy-id "q-106541" :question/problem "Find the axis of symmetry for the parabola $y=-3{x}^{2}-18x+7.$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=a{x}^{2}+bx+c$ is given by\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{b}{2a}.\n$$\n\nWe substitute $a=-3$ and $b=-18$ into the formula for the axis of symmetry. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-\\frac{(-18)}{2(-3)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{(-18)}{(-6)} \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the axis of symmetry is $x=-3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186560972 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083187 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e00837a5-acbf-563d-864a-2902fc8e02a9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vertex of a Parabola"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01b71aec-b8b3-5037-8deb-926f506792fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,15)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560365} {:answer/id #uuid "1e4b65c0-3183-57d2-a3ff-e8e9a1c3a05f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-4,-11)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560433} {:answer/id #uuid "5fab28f4-6451-5564-a2e7-ae3bed8d311e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560569} {:answer/id #uuid "682195de-3e85-5753-851c-879da28ac8bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560582} {:answer/id #uuid "c93d9d5d-d91f-5a40-a5af-007efceb3232" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,-15)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560766}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c93d9d5d-d91f-5a40-a5af-007efceb3232" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,-15)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560766} :answer-field/id #uuid "dca6600a-f1ed-5820-b07a-a9d181dedbc7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560958}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0b6f37ac-511e-531f-9fd9-0e1aa3bfef93" :question/math-academy-id "q-106543" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola $y={x}^{2}+4x-11.$" :question/worked-solution "The vertex of the parabola lies on the axis of symmetry, so we will start by computing the axis of symmetry. \n\nThe equation of the axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=a{x}^{2}+bx+c$ is given by\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{b}{2a}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $a=1$ and $b=4$ into the formula for the axis of symmetry, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-\\frac{4}{2(1)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{2} \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the axis of symmetry is $x=-2.$ This also represents the $x$-coordinate of the vertex. To find the $y$-coordinate of the vertex, we substitute $x=-2$ into the original equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={x}^{2}+4x-11 \\\\  & =(-2)^{2}+4(-2)-11 \\\\  & =4-8-11 \\\\  & =-15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertex is at $(-2,-15).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540089 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083187 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e00837a5-acbf-563d-864a-2902fc8e02a9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vertex of a Parabola"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1546d0b3-484a-554f-a971-19b0784fdf0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,26)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539521} {:answer/id #uuid "388620da-b528-5628-804b-351a30e184bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3,-118)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539583} {:answer/id #uuid "7727e947-2e9c-5fb6-9177-9b23822a088a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,-118)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539678} {:answer/id #uuid "9cddc5f1-bf50-5346-a250-f95ea0170398" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-6,-10)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539738} {:answer/id #uuid "dd0f143d-af04-5bca-8cf5-7e1465de78d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3,26)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539857}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd0f143d-af04-5bca-8cf5-7e1465de78d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3,26)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539857} :answer-field/id #uuid "9031e136-f3f0-5899-8f2b-3f34c3da7fea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539971}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c18c5b5e-e1be-5b37-80b1-242d38a7007c" :question/math-academy-id "q-106548" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola $y=-4{x}^{2}-24x-10.$" :question/worked-solution "The vertex of the parabola lies on the axis of symmetry, so we will start by computing the axis of symmetry. \n\nThe equation of the axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=a{x}^{2}+bx+c$ is given by\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{b}{2a}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $a=-4$ and $b=-24$ into the formula for the axis of symmetry, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-\\frac{(-24)}{2(-4)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{(-24)}{(-8)} \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the axis of symmetry is $x=-3.$ This also represents the $x$-coordinate of the vertex. To find the $y$-coordinate of the vertex, we substitute $x=-3$ into the original equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-4{x}^{2}-24x-10 \\\\  & =-4(-3)^{2}-24(-3)-10 \\\\  & =-36+72-10 \\\\  & =26\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertex is at $(-3,26).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561014 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083188 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e1ed6e03-7d4f-5606-ab01-3bfdd855348e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Unknown Coefficient Given the Axis of Symmetry"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06f09f49-4c97-528f-b8de-3a1879e200e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560376} {:answer/id #uuid "09fcecc3-19a8-57de-9b01-ad29d32f9d14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560386} {:answer/id #uuid "176dee66-a05c-595a-9ab2-46aeebf6b277" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560417} {:answer/id #uuid "428b9f8a-7e89-5114-a895-5026faee9650" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560512} {:answer/id #uuid "74a39713-92e5-576b-b789-33314d80ed36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560613}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "06f09f49-4c97-528f-b8de-3a1879e200e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560376} :answer-field/id #uuid "5bdc9abc-9fd1-5916-ba55-1902c71afb99" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560902}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7198fc6e-53bf-58ce-9c21-b096160c3a27" :question/math-academy-id "q-106550" :question/problem "![](images/9f/9fd54a6b5f5c5c4a711dbdc7de7fcea84177454d6f4a04a1fd647e6a9d93b904.png)\n\nFind the value of $k$ for the parabola $y=-3{x}^{2}+kx+5,$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "First, we will calculate the axis of symmetry in terms of $k.$ Then, since the graph tells us that the axis of symmetry is $x=-1,$ we will set our result equal to $-1.$ \n\nThe equation of the axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=a{x}^{2}+bx+c$ is given by\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{b}{2a}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $a=-3$ and $b=k$ into the formula for the axis of symmetry, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-\\frac{k}{2(-3)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{k}{(-6)} \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe already know that the axis of symmetry is $x=-1,$ so we must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{k}{6} & =-1 \\\\ k & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561032 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083187 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e00837a5-acbf-563d-864a-2902fc8e02a9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vertex of a Parabola"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30b8d0fd-6c5a-5866-938e-4356bd69904e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-6,54)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560471} {:answer/id #uuid "5f89c0ba-747e-5424-b392-8ae56dd31ab5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(6,48)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560568} {:answer/id #uuid "62899510-a87d-5d7f-9a3f-4c33314df94a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3,-75)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560572} {:answer/id #uuid "85daedbc-1998-5aa5-95d2-c689b6aecb21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,50)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560645} {:answer/id #uuid "f256a5f1-0204-5b93-af96-9f80b697b4bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-6,-102)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560844}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f256a5f1-0204-5b93-af96-9f80b697b4bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-6,-102)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560844} :answer-field/id #uuid "2aca8f67-fa9a-544b-9a5d-d25691fbc92b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560877}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9df948ff-fcd8-5687-95bb-a0bdf3f05629" :question/math-academy-id "q-13386" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola $y=3{x}^{2}+36x+6.$" :question/worked-solution "The vertex of the parabola lies on the axis of symmetry, so we will start by computing the axis of symmetry. \n\nThe equation of the axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=a{x}^{2}+bx+c$ is given by\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{b}{2a}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $a=3$ and $b=36$ into the formula for the axis of symmetry, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-\\frac{36}{2(3)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{36}{6} \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the axis of symmetry is $x=-6.$ This also represents the $x$-coordinate of the vertex. To find the $y$-coordinate of the vertex, we substitute $x=-6$ into the original equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3{x}^{2}+36x+6 \\\\  & =3(-6)^{2}+36(-6)+6 \\\\  & =108-216+6 \\\\  & =-102\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertex is at $(-6,-102).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561065 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083186 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "205ecbfe-49fd-559f-a4e7-a36900f1d9c7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Axis of Symmetry of a Parabola"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4295ee61-6048-53f9-9797-3fb92b43b5bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560513}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4295ee61-6048-53f9-9797-3fb92b43b5bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560513} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ac0919c-bc03-5eb1-b683-8e74321045e2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560867}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ff16fd72-aa33-5ed0-9859-414065a202fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-222076" :question/problem "The axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=4{x}^{2}+3x+2$ is $x=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The equation of the axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=a{x}^{2}+bx+c$ is given by\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{b}{2a}.\n$$\n\nWe substitute $a=4$ and $b=3$ into the formula for the axis of symmetry. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-\\frac{3}{2(4)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the axis of symmetry is $x=-\\frac{3}{8}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540082 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083186 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "205ecbfe-49fd-559f-a4e7-a36900f1d9c7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Axis of Symmetry of a Parabola"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "171eba40-f441-599d-bfb0-408b5950a3c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539526}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "171eba40-f441-599d-bfb0-408b5950a3c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539526} :answer-field/id #uuid "70a59569-7026-55cb-8f99-3bedbd6a3b2d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539963}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b00cf238-5726-569e-8376-bed95c1380a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-222079" :question/problem "The axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=-2{x}^{2}+10x-3$ is $x=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The equation of the axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=a{x}^{2}+bx+c$ is given by\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{b}{2a}.\n$$\n\nWe substitute $a=-2$ and $b=10$ into the formula for the axis of symmetry. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-\\frac{10}{2(-2)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{10}{(-4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the axis of symmetry is $x=\\frac{5}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561003 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083187 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e00837a5-acbf-563d-864a-2902fc8e02a9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vertex of a Parabola"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "980f0782-9bf6-5d75-917f-90617c2af852" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560675}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "980f0782-9bf6-5d75-917f-90617c2af852" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560675} :answer-field/id #uuid "bca17f37-d098-5fee-a7b9-8d476bb24f52" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560945} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d25cb9d3-ae1c-5d4b-aad5-470049340353" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560784}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d25cb9d3-ae1c-5d4b-aad5-470049340353" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560784} :answer-field/id #uuid "cab4b1dd-416a-506b-9085-7936c937e72b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560950}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "621c054c-a8ee-5e21-b7c5-55a43d66b230" :question/math-academy-id "q-222082" :question/problem "What are the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola $y={x}^{2}-6x+7?$\n\nThe coordinates of the vertex are\n$($\n{{field-1}}\n,\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" :question/worked-solution "The parabola's vertex lies on the symmetry axis, so we will start by computing the axis of symmetry. \n\nThe equation of the axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=a{x}^{2}+bx+c$ is given by\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{b}{2a}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $a=1$ and $b=-6$ into the formula for the axis of symmetry, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-\\frac{(-6)}{2(1)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{(-6)}{2} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the axis of symmetry is $x=3.$ This also represents the $x$-coordinate of the vertex. To find the $y$-coordinate of the vertex, we substitute $x=3$ into the original equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={x}^{2}-6x+7 \\\\  & ={3}^{2}-6(3)+7 \\\\  & =9-18+7 \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertex is at $(3,-2).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540108 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083188 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e1ed6e03-7d4f-5606-ab01-3bfdd855348e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Unknown Coefficient Given the Axis of Symmetry"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b6f131a8-f416-56ab-b966-abc820357c27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539800}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6f131a8-f416-56ab-b966-abc820357c27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539800} :answer-field/id #uuid "a61a87ea-3783-51c0-97b6-886a2e7f21d3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539978}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f5ac6aea-bcfe-5a0e-83c5-58a351f6e0ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-222095" :question/problem "![](images/8e/8ea5d11ca8b92193517fa7082a466e2ece1f5c505e6881c70ce8ebebb5b93913.png)\n\nFind the value of $k$ for the parabola $y=5{x}^{2}+kx-8,$ shown above.\n\n$k=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we will calculate the axis of symmetry in terms of $k.$ Then, since the graph tells us that the axis of symmetry is $x=-2,$ we will set our result equal to $-2.$ \n\nThe equation of the axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=a{x}^{2}+bx+c$ is given by\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{b}{2a}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $a=5$ and $b=k$ into the formula for the axis of symmetry, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-\\frac{k}{2(5)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{k}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe already know that the axis of symmetry is $x=-2,$ so we must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{k}{10} & =-2 \\\\ -k & =-20 \\\\ k & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561028 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083188 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e1ed6e03-7d4f-5606-ab01-3bfdd855348e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Unknown Coefficient Given the Axis of Symmetry"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18f71e53-c48d-56dc-a20a-a4556c068cbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560421} {:answer/id #uuid "27af2033-5338-514c-8e18-34428ecb9d3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560450} {:answer/id #uuid "2eda800c-a21d-570a-852b-6e5077b553c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560468} {:answer/id #uuid "98059165-843e-5163-a0dc-8950574baeac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560674} {:answer/id #uuid "9e0fa109-40a5-55a1-a241-29a6e4d80bf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560687}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e0fa109-40a5-55a1-a241-29a6e4d80bf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560687} :answer-field/id #uuid "08b63179-28da-5781-a56a-19cfea55072a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560866}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8de5ec05-717f-57d0-aca0-bdf66baf299d" :question/math-academy-id "q-52259" :question/problem "![](images/5c/5cb63eb200d809aa94800fc7990c9a621ad2aca32d86cb1aeb39c844eb9c8205.png)\n\nFind the value of $k$ for the parabola $y=k{x}^{2}+12x-6,$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "First, we will calculate the axis of symmetry in terms of $k.$ Then, since the graph tells us that the axis of symmetry is $x=-3,$ we will set our result equal to $-3.$ \n\nThe equation of the axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=a{x}^{2}+bx+c$ is given by\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{b}{2a}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $a=k$ and $b=12$ into the formula for the axis of symmetry, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-\\frac{12}{2(k)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{12}{2k} \\\\  & =-\\frac{6}{k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe already know that the axis of symmetry is $x=-3,$ so we must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{6}{k} & =-3 \\\\ -6 & =-3k \\\\ k & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561025 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083188 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e1ed6e03-7d4f-5606-ab01-3bfdd855348e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Unknown Coefficient Given the Axis of Symmetry"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d47cbe0-a293-5059-81ae-ce84f00371dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560395} {:answer/id #uuid "2c78fe61-cf74-5dcb-97a3-cd26f9cf105f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560461} {:answer/id #uuid "3bb42019-06df-5498-9d29-49a2aeb6de50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560499} {:answer/id #uuid "8af2d063-d5b4-5386-9515-7976cb518a55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560652} {:answer/id #uuid "a1424b21-9207-5fc2-931a-208860cb0e04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560694}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8af2d063-d5b4-5386-9515-7976cb518a55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560652} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f668b4d-53cc-57b3-995b-4df60daafa74" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560868}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8a434264-115c-5e23-9940-79d2727ed021" :question/math-academy-id "q-52326" :question/problem "The axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=4{x}^{2}+kx-2$ is $x=-1.$ Find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we will calculate the axis of symmetry in terms of $k.$ Then, we will set our result equal to $-1.$ \n\nThe equation of the axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=a{x}^{2}+bx+c$ is given by\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{b}{2a}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $a=4$ and $b=k$ into the formula for the axis of symmetry, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-\\frac{k}{2(4)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{k}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe already know that the axis of symmetry is $x=-1,$ so we must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{k}{8} & =-1 \\\\ -k & =-8 \\\\ k & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186560988 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083188 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e1ed6e03-7d4f-5606-ab01-3bfdd855348e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Unknown Coefficient Given the Axis of Symmetry"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16b90e9b-90ed-511a-9ae3-962fa6391abf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560415} {:answer/id #uuid "1a137401-bd57-566e-9d85-d212c9ba2e04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560425} {:answer/id #uuid "341d0c0d-a5c9-573a-a052-820eab9de3db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560481} {:answer/id #uuid "351bc5d9-a80f-513f-9a55-d9d78db6d7ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560482} {:answer/id #uuid "f1eca14e-bba3-56a3-8702-d07045257425" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560842}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "341d0c0d-a5c9-573a-a052-820eab9de3db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560481} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4d9a73c-49d9-5fa1-8da6-76c9d8ecc11d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560934}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2ea1e232-4156-584c-babd-20b14e2a349e" :question/math-academy-id "q-52329" :question/problem "![](images/5f/5f76e31fbf6e2d7b1398eaafc97e634e955b3314697d650d5f645555c1df289e.png)\n\nFind the value of $k$ for the parabola $y=3{x}^{2}+kx+2$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "First, we will calculate the axis of symmetry in terms of $k.$ Then, since the graph tells us that the axis of symmetry is $x=2,$ we will set our result equal to $2.$ \n\nThe equation of the axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=a{x}^{2}+bx+c$ is given by\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{b}{2a}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $a=3$ and $b=k$ into the formula for the axis of symmetry, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-\\frac{k}{2(3)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{k}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe already know that the axis of symmetry is $x=2,$ so we must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{k}{6} & =2 \\\\ k & =-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
